# Review ownership.
#
# A single maintainer means this does not change who reviews what -- it requests
# the same reviewer either way. It is here for the second reason: it names the
# paths where a change is a **boundary** change rather than a feature, so a
# contributor can see before opening a pull request which files need an argument
# rather than a description.

# Default: everything.
*                       @immutex

# --- Security boundaries -------------------------------------------------------
# A change here alters what the harness claims to enforce. `SECURITY.md` §For
# contributors applies: the commit should name the layer, and a boundary change
# needs a test that fails without it.
#
# /src/mcode/perm/          the permission engine and the hard-deny floor
# /src/mcode/platform/      the three OS sandboxes
# /src/mcode/ext/api_gate   the extension capability boundary
/src/mcode/perm/        @immutex
/src/mcode/platform/    @immutex
/src/mcode/ext/api_gate.cxx  @immutex
/src/mcode/ext/api_gate.hxx  @immutex
/src/mcode/ext/loader.cxx    @immutex
/src/mcode/ext/manifest.cxx  @immutex
SECURITY.md             @immutex

# --- Budgets -------------------------------------------------------------------
# These define the numbers every other decision is measured against. Changing one
# is a design change, not an edit: `docs/01-north-star.md` is the single source of
# truth and moves first, then every doc that cites it.
/docs/01-north-star.md  @immutex
/docs/40-non-obvious-constraints.md  @immutex

# --- Release and supply chain --------------------------------------------------
# The installers execute a downloaded binary, so a change here is a supply-chain
# change: verification must happen before anything runs.
/install.ps1            @immutex
/install.sh             @immutex
/.github/workflows/     @immutex
/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md @immutex
/LICENSE                @immutex
